    "turn_text": "Well, we don't really know because, you know, it's a privacy issue, but it's 25% of the members of the house, according to the survey have not have refused to take the vaccine. So this makes it very difficult for us to operate. I'll give you another example. You know, went to a funeral, a guy who's a friend of mine who owns a funeral home, and he says that people make decisions about whether to mask way of mass at the funeral based on ideology. So like if he's in a town where it's mostly Republican, a lot of the people kind of the funeral pollen refused to wear a mask. On the other hand, if a democratic town, they wear a mask. So it's absurd. But I mean, this is what happens. But I think you just got to, you know, you just got to try to overcome it as best you can. But it's not easy. I'm not, I'm not this degree in what you state.",
